{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1420353-a-heroes-campaign-for-the-new-england-region-running-an-amusement-park","id":1420353,"title":"A heroes campaign for the New England region. Running an Amusement Park.","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","Scion"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-10-26T17:19:21-07:00","id":1420353,"title":"A heroes campaign for the New England region. Running an Amusement Park.","content":"The idea may sound odd, but the Pantheons of the Northeastern USA are supposed to be very ready to engage the modern world and pragmatically innovative, especially the Manitou. So, the idea is that a Demigod of another pantheon (I haven't decided which other pantheon but the Demigod is strong in Prosperity and Luck) gives an impoverished band of Native Americans living on or near the shores of Lake Champlain an amusement park. The park was built on land stolen from the ancestors of this band, and the Demigod loves to return long lost or stolen property to the rightful owners. <br /> <br /> The PCs are a group of scions, heroes just starting out, tasked with making the Park a success in several ways...<br /> <br /> A) A financial success to restore self-sufficiency to those the land was stolen from.<br /> <br /> B) Make it a way to teach native culture and mythology to the general public without degrading or oversimplifying these things. <br /> <br /> C) Prevent traditionalist purists from being hyper-offended at the idea of the local band running an amusement park.<br /> <br /> D) Defend the park from enemies of all kinds. <br /> <br /> The Park in Question is called Storybook Land and it is on the shores of <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lake_Champlain\" target=\"_blank\">Lake Champlain</a>. The park is in good physical condition but it's themed in terms of the most commonly known Fairy Tales in America with great care to avoid offending Disney's copywrite lawyers. <br /> <br /> So, what ideas would you guys add?<br /> <br /> Note: If you hate the whole thing, please don't post. <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-27T00:22:50-07:00","id":1420413,"title":"","content":"Don\u2019t have a god from another pantheon give the park to the band. That\u2019s too much like a white savior thing. Make it one of the Manitou gods.<br /> <br /> Don\u2019t make it European fairy tales like Disneyland. Why would the Manitou care about preserving the fairy tales of the people who conquered them? Use authentic Iroquois/Algonquin myths and legends.<br /> <br /> That being said, I think B is a great idea for a band of Manitou Scions. It would make a pretty cool home base for your band.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-27T03:45:44-07:00","id":1420425,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Penelope</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1420353-a-heroes-campaign-for-the-new-england-region-running-an-amusement-park?p=1420413#post1420413\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Don\u2019t have a god from another pantheon give the park to the band. That\u2019s too much like a white savior thing. Make it one of the Manitou gods.<br /> <br /> Don\u2019t make it European fairy tales like Disneyland. Why would the Manitou care about preserving the fairy tales of the people who conquered them? Use authentic Iroquois/Algonquin myths and legends.<br /> <br /> That being said, I think B is a great idea for a band of Manitou Scions. It would make a pretty cool home base for your band.</div> </div> </div> </div>The European fairy tales theme and design is a problem for the PCs to overcome. <br /> <br /> As to the giver, perhaps they are from another Native American pantheon.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-27T10:50:33-07:00","id":1420516,"title":"","content":"Another way to avoid the White Savior stereotype is to not make the patron white. Celestial Bureaucracy, Kami, Orisha, etc. are all choices that could work in that respect.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-27T10:56:59-07:00","id":1420517,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1420353-a-heroes-campaign-for-the-new-england-region-running-an-amusement-park?p=1420516#post1420516\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Another way to avoid the White Savior stereotype is to not make the patron white. Celestial Bureaucracy, Kami, Orisha, etc. are all choices that could work in that respect.</div> </div> </div> </div>Great idea.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-27T11:53:14-07:00","id":1420528,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1420353-a-heroes-campaign-for-the-new-england-region-running-an-amusement-park?p=1420516#post1420516\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Another way to avoid the White Savior stereotype is to not make the patron white. Celestial Bureaucracy, Kami, Orisha, etc. are all choices that could work in that respect.</div> </div> </div> </div>The giver simply returned stolen property. An act of decency. Since when is decency a violation of others? Anyone who came into procession of long ago stolen property (in this case the lakeside land the park is built on) would, if they met a basic standard of decency, return said property to the rightful owners. Saying the Giver, or more aptly the Restorer is a &quot;White Savior&quot; seems exaggerated. More like I'm being accused of immorality than discussing ideas for a game.<br /> <br /> Let's drop the subject. And move on to other aspects of the setting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-27T12:03:40-07:00","id":1420530,"title":"","content":"Try this for a problem. The PCs and an ally have the puppet theater running. The puppets are lovely interpretations of Native American art and culturally accurate depictions of Mythic and folkloric beings from local legend. The puppeteers and musicians are from the local band. The stories performed are based on local myths and legends and representative of both their culture's storytelling style and sense of humor. And they are a hit. <br /> <br /> Sure, the puppet theater is in a very eurocentric looking storybook castle. But they don't have the cash to change that yet.<br /> <br /> A far more serious problem is that some of the creatures depicted in the plays want to see them. These creatures are known to be easily offended and very violent. <br /> <br /> Art meets diplomacy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-27T22:23:36-07:00","id":1420613,"title":"","content":"An infamous Scion of Huehuecoyotl (or any other god of orgies, drunkenness and partying), who may or may not actually be a Titanspawn in disguise, visits the park together with a cult of revelers. Soon they spread chaos and disorder with their insane partying and the number of visitors dwindle quickly. Of course the cops are called, but using Trickster Knacks and the different Purviews the Scion constantly shifts blame around, complicates and stalls any kind of action by the authorities.<br /> <br /> It is now up to the PCs themselves to take care of this problem. They must try to find out why this Scion is so bent on ruining their amusement park and stop them, hopefully without angering any gods in the process.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9849-aristarkos","name":"Aristarkos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9849_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-28T01:39:33-07:00","id":1420635,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aristarkos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1420353-a-heroes-campaign-for-the-new-england-region-running-an-amusement-park?p=1420613#post1420613\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">An infamous Scion of Huehuecoyotl (or any other god of orgies, drunkenness and partying), who may or may not actually be a Titanspawn in disguise, visits the park together with a cult of revelers. Soon they spread chaos and disorder with their insane partying and the number of visitors dwindle quickly. Of course the cops are called, but using Trickster Knacks and the different Purviews the Scion constantly shifts blame around, complicates and stalls any kind of action by the authorities.<br /> <br /> It is now up to the PCs themselves to take care of this problem. They must try to find out why this Scion is so bent on ruining their amusement park and stop them, hopefully without angering any gods in the process.</div> </div> </div> </div>Good idea. Even without paranormal powers the party hardy crowd are a threat to any family park.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-28T03:54:28-07:00","id":1420645,"title":"","content":"No one wants their makeout session on the Ferris Wheel disturbed by drunken revelers \ud83d\ude0a<br /> <br /> Seriously. As long as you don\u2019t make it too Eurocentric this could be a great home base for a Manitou band.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-28T14:31:01-07:00","id":1420715,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Penelope</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1420353-a-heroes-campaign-for-the-new-england-region-running-an-amusement-park?p=1420645#post1420645\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No one wants their makeout session on the Ferris Wheel disturbed by drunken revelers \ud83d\ude0a<br /> <br /> Seriously. As long as you don\u2019t make it too Eurocentric this could be a great home base for a Manitou band.</div> </div> </div> </div>But undoing the eurocentristy of the park is one of the problems. To start with, they've got the problem of creating a look for the park which isn't a rehash of &quot;cigar store Indian&quot; cliches. Not an easy problem. Plus the expense of massive rebuilding.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-28T15:28:42-07:00","id":1420719,"title":"","content":"Why did you choose Lake Champlain? Does it have a special significance for the story?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10624-sacerdos","name":"Sacerdos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10624_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"231"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-28T17:42:45-07:00","id":1420733,"title":"","content":"Oh I simply think it's a beautiful lake. But older amusement parks tended to be built near lakes. Lake Champlain is a very large lake and one of America's most beautiful lakes. It's known as a vacation area, and it's close, relatively, to New York, Boston, Montreal, Providence, and other interesting places. <br /> <br /> It's just a useful choice.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-28T22:08:10-07:00","id":1420769,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Astromancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1420353-a-heroes-campaign-for-the-new-england-region-running-an-amusement-park?p=1420733#post1420733\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh I simply think it's a beautiful lake. But older amusement parks tended to be built near lakes. Lake Champlain is a very large lake and one of America's most beautiful lakes. It's known as a vacation area, and it's close, relatively, to New York, Boston, Montreal, Providence, and other interesting places.<br /> <br /> It's just a useful choice.</div> </div> </div> </div>Would there be Denizens and other things inside the lake? Mermaids? Underwater cave? Miraculous healing water?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9849-aristarkos","name":"Aristarkos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9849_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-29T00:42:31-07:00","id":1420781,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aristarkos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1420353-a-heroes-campaign-for-the-new-england-region-running-an-amusement-park?p=1420769#post1420769\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Would there be Denizens and other things inside the lake? Mermaids? Underwater cave? Miraculous healing water?</div> </div> </div> </div>Of course. These things are part of Native American myth too.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-29T02:06:55-07:00","id":1420788,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Astromancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1420353-a-heroes-campaign-for-the-new-england-region-running-an-amusement-park?p=1420781#post1420781\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Of course. These things are part of Native American myth too.</div> </div> </div> </div>There's in fact a specific kind of Anishinaabe merfolk that you could populate the lake with, if you want. They're called Nebaunaubaewuk, if you want to look into them. It's part of the reason why I asked whether you had chosen the lake for any specific folklore already attached to it. Lake Champlain is technically outside traditional Anishinaabe lands, so using the Manidoog is a bit of a stretch, but they're what the game offers, and it's close enough geographically that I personally think inventing an outlier band or something isn't too unreasonable if you're attached to that specific lake. Wiki also claims there have been tales of a monster in the lake since Champlain himself, so that sounds like another cool element to use if it's true. My immediate thought would be that the monster decides to become a mascot/protector to the park once it is in Native hands again.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10624-sacerdos","name":"Sacerdos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10624_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"231"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-29T05:05:55-07:00","id":1420799,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aristarkos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1420353-a-heroes-campaign-for-the-new-england-region-running-an-amusement-park?p=1420769#post1420769\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Would there be Denizens and other things inside the lake? Mermaids? Underwater cave? Miraculous healing water?</div> </div> </div> </div>I love it \ud83d\ude0a","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-29T18:07:57-07:00","id":1420907,"title":"","content":"Try these ideas...<br /> <br /> Remembering that Apollo has aspects that are best summed up as &quot;the Wolf Hunter&quot; and &quot;the Werewolf.&quot; Fairly closely related relatives could take after different aspects of the god. Which would make family gathering rather more...lively.<br /> <br /> The Daystar Inn is a large medium-priced hotel (it routinely wins prizes for &quot;best family hotel in New England&quot;, or &quot;best hotel bargain in New England&quot;) and fairly near the Amusement park. The people who stay there are a major source of customers for the Amusement Park. However, the family that owns the Inn has two Scions of Apollo, both of whom feel they should have a controlling interest in the Inn. Aton White reflects the Wolf-Hunter aspect and his cousin Lawrence Black is a werewolf (a rare non-titan spawn werewolf, a Limmular Anarchist Trickster). The fight threatens to both destroy the Inn and damage the Park's economic viability.<br /> <br /> This is a delicate job in diplomacy. Made much harder by the fact that both of the cousins are insufferable. Aton genuinely wants to be one of the good guys, and he works <i>hard</i> so very hard, to be a decent ally. But his privileged background always shows through in a deeply irritating way. Meanwhile, Lawrence is an enthusiastic political and cultural radical whose embrace of his &quot;Brown Brothers&quot; is as irritating as it is obsessively politically correct. Note: If the PCs are Origin level characters, the cousins are Heroes, if the PCs are heroes, the Cousins are Demigods.<br /> <br /> <br /> More tomorrow I must go.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":857,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","user":"Astromancer","date":". 12-31-2024, 10:31 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-30T18:43:52-07:00","id":1421080,"title":"","content":"It is tomorrow...<br /> <br /> New pavements have been laid in many areas of the park. These rather handsome new pavements are patterned after traditional beadwork. These pavements represent a major step in the process of rebranding and transforming the park away from the present Eurocentric look and toward a look that fits the cultures of New England's Native American groups. <br /> <br /> However, a crisis has turned up. A woman from a small tribal group is furious. The patterns are sacred to her people and walking on them is a profanation! She's about the only living speaker of her people's language and among the few who still follow their ancient faith (almost all the others are Congregationalists). Many of her relatives say she is a serial fabulist and often makes up things to push people around or get attention, But in this case, it's very hard to tell.<br /> <br /> Tearing up the pavements would be far too expensive and would prevent the opening of the park for most of the season. It would break the park. <br /> <br /> The PCs need to visit the Terra Incognita of this woman's people and learn the truth. <br /> <br /> More later. <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}